                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "zQmyU",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 24,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "j7N332",
                  "name": "Scoop installs pond as a portable zip: t",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 238,
                  "content": "Scoop installs pond as a portable zip: the shim puts pond on PATH, the bucket updates itself from each GitHub release, and scoop update pond upgrades in place. What it fetches is pond-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip (~77 MB download, ~223 MB unpacked), attached to every release. No Scoop at all? Unpack that zip anywhere, put the directory on PATH, and you are done - nothing else to install. The build is x86_64; on Windows 11 on ARM it installs and runs under the built-in x64 emulation (Windows 10 on ARM has no x64 emulation, and Scoop resolves it to a 32-bit entry this manifest does not carry). winget is not available yet - the manifest is in review; winget install tenequm.pond starts working once it merges.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "WUKV7",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "l79xU",
                  "name": "Already have a Rust toolchain? cargo bin",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 96,
                  "content": "Already have a Rust toolchain? cargo binstall pond-db fetches the same prebuilt zip with no git, protoc, or NASM involved - but it installs pond.exe only, so scheduled sync (which runs through pondw.exe) needs the Scoop or zip install.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "YkJgU",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "hK4Kj",
                  "name": "Installed with an agent session already ",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 90,
                  "content": "Installed with an agent session already running? The new PATH entry reaches only processes started after the install - open a fresh terminal (and restart the agent client) if pond reports not found.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "R3gM3",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Trydu",
                  "name": "The zip carries completion scripts for P",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 206,
                  "content": "The zip carries completion scripts for PowerShell, bash, zsh, and fish. Register the PowerShell one by dot-sourcing it from your $PROFILE; with Scoop the file is at ~\\scoop\\apps\\pond\\current\\completions\\_pond.ps1. On a fresh machine $PROFILE may not exist yet - create it first with if (!(Test-Path $PROFILE)) { New-Item -ItemType File -Path $PROFILE -Force | Out-Null } (a bare New-Item -Force would truncate an existing profile).",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "fc6Dv",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "p5vQum",
                  "name": "Building from source instead needs two t",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 90,
                  "content": "Building from source instead needs two tools the prebuilt binary spares you: protoc, because protobuf-src cannot vendor it on Windows, and NASM, for aws-lc-sys. Embeddings, if you enable them, run on the CPU backend.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "uuRwa",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "xTKMJ",
                  "name": "h3",
                  "context": "h3",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 36,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    13,
                    0,
                    0,
                    0
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "VLrne",
                      "name": "Scheduled sync",
                      "fill": "#ffffff",
                      "content": "Scheduled sync",
                      "lineHeight": 1,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 20,
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "letterSpacing": -0.5
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "L2tX3p",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "t4jrwj",
                  "name": "pond schedule start registers a Task Sch",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 186,
                  "content": "pond schedule start registers a Task Scheduler job. Run it from a normal shell, not an elevated one: a task registered elevated is owned by Administrators, and every later pond schedule start/stop from a normal shell fails with Access denied (pond warns before registering elevated, and the error names the recovery if you're already caught). After moving pond between install channels - a manual zip to Scoop, say - run pond schedule start once so the task points at the new binaries; pond status flags a registration whose launcher no longer exists.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "jRuRS",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "HY5UU",
                  "name": "h3",
                  "context": "h3",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 36,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    13,
                    0,
                    0,
                    0
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "Jnl3H",
                      "name": "Over SSH",
                      "fill": "#ffffff",
                      "content": "Over SSH",
                      "lineHeight": 1,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 20,
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "letterSpacing": -0.5
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "Or2sP",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "OchTO",
                  "name": "A bucket install's shim works over SSH -",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 180,
                  "content": "A bucket install's shim works over SSH - pond resolves and spawns from remote PowerShell, cmd, and Git Bash sessions alike (inside WSL, call it as pond.exe: interop appends the Windows PATH but does not infer the extension). If yours fails with \"Could not create process\" while local shells work fine, the shim itself is stale - seen once with a shim created by a hand-pinned manifest install - and reinstalling from the bucket (scoop uninstall pond; scoop install tenequm/pond) regenerates it. As a stopgap, call the exe directly: ~\\scoop\\apps\\pond\\current\\pond.exe.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "v3I0b",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "n4YFXF",
                  "name": "h3",
                  "context": "h3",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 36,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    13,
                    0,
                    0,
                    0
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "RC5S1",
                      "name": "Defender and where the store lives",
                      "fill": "#ffffff",
                      "content": "Defender and where the store lives",
                      "lineHeight": 1,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 20,
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "letterSpacing": -0.5
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "qSig8",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "taySR",
                  "name": "A pond store is many small files, and De",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 252,
                  "content": "A pond store is many small files, and Defender's real-time scanning charges per file touched - excluding pond's directory (%LOCALAPPDATA%\\pond by default, holding the store, cache, and state) is worth it if sync or search feels slow. Keep the store on an NTFS volume: local stores commit through a hard-link-and-rename dance that NTFS documents and pond has verified there, while ReFS volumes - including Dev Drive - are unverified for that path. A UNC path is rejected outright at the store URL, because the layers underneath silently drop the host component and the store would open somewhere else; a mapped network drive has the same fault but cannot be told apart from a local drive, so pond cannot reject it for you - point the store at a local drive or a remote scheme (s3://, gs://, az://).",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "sA2zS",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "cSUok",
                  "name": "h3",
                  "context": "h3",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 36,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    13,
                    0,
                    0,
                    0
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "q67vJk",
                      "name": "Long paths",
                      "fill": "#ffffff",
                      "content": "Long paths",
                      "lineHeight": 1,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 20,
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "letterSpacing": -0.5
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "DR4Am",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "d3AS7",
                  "name": "The Windows binary ships a manifest decl",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 232,
                  "content": "The Windows binary ships a manifest declaring long-path awareness, which only takes effect on machines where the LongPathsEnabled policy is also set. Nothing in pond's own path handling depends on it - it is insurance for the bundled C libraries and for tools pond spawns. Cloning this repository is the one case that genuinely needs it, and needs it in git rather than in pond: git config --global core.longpaths true - some test fixtures nest encoded project slugs past 260 characters. Build and test from a clone with an explicit --target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc; without it cargo applies the repo's +crt-static flag to build scripts and proc-macros too, which then fail to load.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "R41ee",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "cmlgU",
                  "name": "h3",
                  "context": "h3",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 36,
                  "layout": "vertical",
                  "padding": [
                    13,
                    0,
                    0,
                    0
                  ],
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "id": "FHEQ0",
                      "name": "WSL",
                      "fill": "#ffffff",
                      "content": "WSL",
                      "lineHeight": 1,
                      "fontFamily": "Geist",
                      "fontSize": 20,
                      "fontWeight": "500",
                      "letterSpacing": -0.5
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "iAmP1",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 16,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "b2bqAm",
                  "name": "Running the Linux binary under WSL works",
                  "context": "p",
                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 84,
                  "content": "Running the Linux binary under WSL works when both the agent session files and the pond store live on the ext4 side. Do not point either across /mnt/c: throughput collapses and Windows-side writes are missed.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                  "fontSize": 16,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "Ax8rx",
                  "name": "spacer",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 40,
                  "layout": "none"
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "k9jPh",
