                                  "layout": "vertical",
                                  "children": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "frame",
                                      "id": "JgGKG",
                                      "name": "div",
                                      "context": "div",
                                      "clip": true,
                                      "width": "fill_container",
                                      "height": 600,
                                      "layout": "vertical",
                                      "children": [
                                        {
                                          "type": "frame",
                                          "id": "Umt76",
                                          "name": "div",
                                          "context": "Je - div",
                                          "width": "fill_container",
                                          "height": 990,
                                          "layout": "vertical",
                                          "gap": 16,
                                          "children": [
                                            {
                                              "type": "text",
                                              "id": "e9TH20",
                                              "name": "The storage engine moves to Lance 14.0.2",
                                              "context": "p",
                                              "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                                              "width": "fill_container",
                                              "height": 130,
                                              "content": "The storage engine moves to Lance 14.0.2. Full-text search reads up to three quarters fewer bytes per query, and unfiltered row counts come straight from table metadata. Lance 14 keeps BTree index entries as row addresses, which an older writer would silently corrupt, so this release fences older writers off every store it writes.",
                                              "lineHeight": 1.63,
                                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                                              "fontSize": 16,
                                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "text",
                                              "id": "m2MOxm",
                                              "name": "Upgrading: upgrade every host that reads",
                                              "context": "p",
                                              "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                                              "width": "fill_container",
                                              "height": 582,
                                              "content": "Upgrading: upgrade every host that reads or writes a shared store, within your agents' session-retention window (Claude Code keeps 30 days by default), and restart anything that keeps pond running, such as an OpenClaw, pi or Hermes plugin host or pond serve: a running process keeps its old binary. Upgrade pond 0.18 and older first. Their Lance checks the fence only on appends, so their optimize and copy writes still land: they erase the fence and swap the new BTree indexes for older-format ones. Nothing is lost, but every swap costs a full index rebuild, and until a host on this release writes again, pond 0.19 and 0.20 can write too. Once any host on this release has synced, optimized or copied into the store, pond 0.19 and 0.20 still read it correctly but more slowly (search up to about 9x slower on a 22 GB store, close to the 60-second tool timeouts some MCP clients use), and each write they attempt fails with \"This dataset cannot be written by this version of Lance\" until they upgrade. Their pond optimize may instead report a \"structural index fault\" and suggest pond optimize --rebuild: ignore that hint, which is refused the same way and loses nothing, and upgrade. The first index pass on this release (a pond optimize, or a pond sync once enough new rows arrive) rebuilds the five BTree indexes once from a full scan: 36 seconds at a 423 MB peak on a 22 GB store. pond mcp on a store no sync has created yet exits naming pond sync; after that sync, restart the MCP client.",
                                              "lineHeight": 1.63,
                                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                                              "fontSize": 16,
                                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "text",
                                              "id": "czUii",
                                              "name": "🛠 Breaking Changes",
                                              "context": "h3",
                                              "fill": "#ffffff",
                                              "content": "🛠 Breaking Changes",
                                              "lineHeight": 1,
                                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                                              "fontSize": 20,
                                              "fontWeight": "500",
                                              "letterSpacing": -0.5
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "frame",
                                              "id": "XoDsb",
                                              "name": "ul",
                                              "context": "ul",
                                              "width": "fill_container",
                                              "layout": "vertical",
                                              "padding": [
                                                0,
                                                0,
                                                0,
                                                24
                                              ],
                                              "children": [
                                                {
                                                  "type": "text",
                                                  "id": "dQClW",
                                                  "name": "[breaking] upgrade Lance to 14.0.2 (#370",
                                                  "context": "li",
                                                  "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                                                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                                                  "width": "fill_container",
                                                  "height": 142,
                                                  "content": "[breaking] upgrade Lance to 14.0.2 (#370) (9e386bf) Pond now runs on Lance 14.0.2. Once a host on this release writes a store, pond 0.19 and 0.20 can still read it but not write it; upgrade pond 0.18 and older first. pond mcp now opens the store read-only: on a new or older-schema store it asks you to run pond sync first.",
                                                  "lineHeight": 1.63,
                                                  "fontFamily": "Geist",
                                                  "fontSize": 16,
                                                  "fontWeight": "normal",
                                                  "letterSpacing": 0.08
                                                }
                                              ]
                                            },
                                            {
                                              "type": "text",
                                              "id": "ZGdQJ",
                                              "name": "Full Changelog: https://github.com/teneq",
                                              "context": "p",
                                              "fill": "#e9e9e9",
                                              "textGrowth": "fixed-width-height",
                                              "width": "fill_container",
                                              "height": 52,
                                              "content": "Full Changelog: https://github.com/tenequm/pond/compare/v0.20.3...v0.21.0",
                                              "lineHeight": 1.63,
                                              "fontFamily": "Geist",
                                              "fontSize": 16,
                                              "fontWeight": "normal"
                                            }
                                          ]
                                        }
                                      ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                      "type": "frame",
                                      "id": "D3pUu",
                                      "layoutPosition": "absolute",
                                      "x": 0,
                                      "y": 494,
